---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MembershipTiers from '../components/MembershipTiers.tsx';
---

<BaseLayout title="Heredita — Membership">
  <main class="container" style="padding-top: 22px;">
    <section class="text-center reveal" style="padding: 20px 12px 4px;">
      <h1 class="tilt-l" style="font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.6rem); margin-bottom: 4px;">Membership</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto;">
        Three tiers. Pricing will be announced when the Store opens — for now, pick the one that sounds like you and we'll let you know.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MembershipTiers client:load />

    <p class="muted text-center reveal" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      Want to preview a tier? Use the <a href="/settings">Settings page</a> to switch your local profile.
    </p>

    <div class="section-title reveal" style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <h2 class="tilt-r">FAQ</h2>
      <span class="muted">questions we keep getting</span>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-grid">
      <div class="chalk-card reveal">
        <h3>What's the difference between Guest and Regular?</h3>
        <p>Gameplay is exactly the same. Regular members get a profile, monthly Heredita Coins, and the free seasonal hat — but you can do everything Regular can do as a Guest, minus the goodies.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal">
        <h3>The free hat — really free?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Every Regular account auto-claims a top hat the first time they open the site. It stays on your avatar forever, but the claim window closes <strong>Aug 28, 2026</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal">
        <h3>What can Emperor do that Regular can't?</h3>
        <p>Host private servers with 30+ players, get a sign-in bonus + bigger monthly drop, a one-time rare-item lottery spin, and a custom chat tag with their own name color.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal">
        <h3>Will my saves stay forever?</h3>
        <p>Right now everyone has unlimited saves. After launch, non-Emperor accounts will be limited to 5 saved timelines. Emperors keep unlimited.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
